{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,70p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '1,65p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc; sed -n '260,280p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc; sed -n '435,478p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc; sed -n '137,160p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/link_test.cljc; sed -n '409,430p' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc; sed -n '391,415p' test/yin/vm/heap_reclamation_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,70p' docs/design/datom.world.md; sed -n '1,65p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc; sed -n '260,280p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc; sed -n '435,478p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/effects_test.cljc; sed -n '137,160p' test/yin/vm/semantic_register/link_test.cljc; sed -n '409,430p' src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic_register.cljc; sed -n '391,415p' test/yin/vm/heap_reclamation_test.cljc\"","aggregated_output":"---\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\n---\n\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\n\n## Core Philosophy\n\nEverything is data.\nInterpretation > abstraction.\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\nRestrictions are a feature.\n\n### Foundational Axioms\n\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: All IO and data flow through append-only streams.\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\n   At system scale, a \"system\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime execution state are structured datoms, enabling syntax independence and structural reflection.\n4. **Everything is a Continuation**: Computation is modeled as serializable, portable continuations that can pause, travel across streams, and resume anywhere.\n\n## Non-Negotiable Invariants\n\n- Do not introduce hidden global state.\n- Do not introduce implicit control flow.\n- Do not introduce callbacks; every callback is an event on a stream.\n- Do not introduce shared mutable state.\n- Do not collapse interpretation and execution into the same layer.\n- Do not assume graphs: graphs must be constructed explicitly from tuples.\n- Do not lose information (unitarity): streams are append-only and no datom is destroyed, only reinterpreted. The Universal AST is never lost: it is always retrievable wherever code is lowered, by address or by a query over its datoms. Every derived form (semantic vector, native images, indexes) is an interpretation of it and may drop facts only because the AST remains.\n\n## Tuples and Datoms\n\nTuples are elements in an open moduli space, graded by dimension $n$. A tuple can be any dimension/size.\nA datom is the canonical persistent tuple `[e a v t m]` (entity, attribute, value, transaction, metadata). Persistent facts are immutable datoms.\nSource scope belongs to the interpreter, never to an appended tuple slot. Queries keep physical sources as separate db-values and express union or joins explicitly.\n\nSee [`docs/design/datom.md`](./datom.md) for full specification.\n\n## Streams\n\nAll IO is modeled as a stream. Functions consume streams and produce streams.\nNo direct function-to-function coupling without a stream boundary.\nSide effects must appear as stream emissions.\nStreams are values that can be sent through streams.\nStreams carry whatever values the consumer needs: no datom requirement, no privileged payload shape.\n\nA stream has no privileged reader, and its meaning is not in it. Any number\nof interpreters may observe the same medium, and each constructs its own\nsemantics from the same batches: a `yin.vm` evaluator observing a program\nstream constructs CESK state and executes it; `dao.space.index` observing\nthe very same stream materializes covered indexes, so `dao.space.query/q`\nanswers Datalog over the program as it grows. Neither knows the other\nexists. The medium is their only coupling, and each observer's ignorance of\nthe other is load-bearing: the evaluator never consults an index to run,\nand the index never evaluates a form to index it. This is how axiom 2\nbecomes architecture: one stream, many interpretations, none of them\nthe stream's own.\n\nFunctions can take anything and return anything.\nAgents are functions, closures, or continuations in `yin.vm` that communicate with the outside world through `dao.stream`. Agent behavior is specified entirely through stream effects.\n\nSee [`docs/design/dao.stream.md`](./dao.stream.md) for full stream specification.\nSee [`docs/design/yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md`](./yin.vm.streams-all-the-way-down.md) for VM architecture.\n\n### Host Boundaries\n\nA host boundary is a stream boundary, never a function call. The one\n(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.effects-test\n  (:require [clojure.edn :as edn]\n            [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.ast-walker :as walker]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.walker-trace-test :as trace]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :refer [lit v lam app tail if-node def!]]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.parity-test :as parity]))\n\n\n(defn run-ast\n  ([ast] (vm/run (parity/register-machine ast {:env {'vector vector}})))\n  ([machine ast] (vm/run (sr/load-ast machine (vm/ast->datoms ast) vm/ast-contract))))\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e\n                 {:message (ex-message e) :data (ex-data e)})))\n\n\n(defn until-inst\n  [machine op]\n  (loop [machine machine fuel 1000]\n    (when (zero? fuel) (throw (ex-info \"Test did not reach instruction\" {:op op})))\n    (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control machine)\n          inst (nth (get-in machine [:code segment :vector]) pc)]\n      (if (= op (first inst)) machine (recur (vm/step machine) (dec fuel))))))\n\n\n(defn next-node\n  [cursor]\n  {:type :stream/next :source cursor})\n\n\n(defn put-node\n  [s x]\n  {:type :stream/put :target s :val x})\n\n\n(defn cursor-node\n  [s]\n  {:type :stream/cursor :source s})\n\n\n(defn reader\n  []\n  (parity/register-machine (next-node (cursor-node {:type :stream/make :buffer 4}))))\n\n\n(defn reader-with-live-window\n  []\n  (parity/register-machine\n    (app (v 'vector) (lit nil) (next-node (cursor-node {:type :stream/make :buffer 4})) (lit 2))\n    {:env {'vector vector}}))\n\n(deftest store-and-gensym-test\n  (let [ast (app (v 'vector) {:type :vm/gensym} {:type :stream/make :buffer 4} {:type :vm/gensym :prefix \"g\"})\n        done (run-ast ast) [a s b] (vm/value done)]\n    (is (= :id-0 a)) (is (= :stream-1 (:id s))) (is (= :g-2 b))\n    (is (= 3 (:id-counter done)))))\n\n\n(deftest window-is-a-gc-root\n  (let [modules (module/register-cell-module (module/default-registry))\n        result (vm/run (parity/register-machine (app (v 'vector) (app (v 'cell/new) (lit :keep)) (app (v 'cell/new) (lit :junk))) {:modules modules :env {'vector vector}}))\n        [keep-ref] (vm/value result)\n        only-window (assoc result :env {} :control nil :k nil :value nil :window {0 keep-ref})\n        collected (engine/collect only-window)]\n    (is (= #{:keep} (set (map :value (vals (:heap collected))))))\n    (is (= #{} (set (map :value (vals (:heap (engine/collect (assoc only-window :window {}))))))))))\n\n\n;; The five continuation programs are respelled here; backend registration is stage 2.\n(def capture {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n\n\n    (is (= 7 (:dao.stream/value (stream/next handle cursor)))))\n  (is (some? (error #(run-ast (put-node (lit {:type :stream-ref :id :missing}) (lit 1)))))))\n\n\n(defn ffi-node\n  [op & operands]\n  {:type :dao.stream.apply/call :op op :operands (vec operands)})\n\n\n(defn ffi-program\n  []\n  (app (v 'vector) (lit nil) (ffi-node :op/echo (lit 7)) (lit 2)))\n\n\n(deftest ffi-sent\n  (let [before (until-inst (parity/register-machine (ffi-program)\n                                                    {:env {'vector vector} :ffi-caller-id :caller}) :ffi-call)\n        {:keys [segment pc]} (:control before)\n        rd (second (nth (get-in before [:code segment :vector]) pc))\n        blocked (vm/step before) entry (first (:wait-set blocked)) call-id (:call-id entry)]\n    (is (vm/blocked? blocked))\n    (is (nil? (:control blocked))) (is (nil? (:k blocked)))\n    (is (= [:caller :parked-0] call-id))\n    (is (= :next (:reason entry)))\n    (is (= {1 vector 2 nil} (:window entry)))\n    (is (= {:deliver :rd :rd 3} (:deliver entry)))\n    (is (= rd 3))\n    (is (= (inc pc) (:pc entry)))\n    (is (= (:env before) (:env entry)))\n    (is (= (select-keys (:window before) (analysis/saved (get-in before [:code segment :analysis]) (inc pc) rd))\n           (:window entry)))\n    (is (not-any? #(contains? entry %) [:datom :request-sent :op]))\n    (is (= (select-keys entry [:segment :pc :env :window :k :deliver])\n           (select-keys (get (:parked blocked) call-id) [:segment :pc :env :window :k :deliver])))\n    (let [bridge (ffi/bridge-step (ffi/attach blocked {:op/echo identity}))\n          ready (engine/check-wait-set (:vm bridge))\n          restored (engine/resume-from-run-queue ready sr/register-restore)]\n      (is (:handled? bridge))\n      (is (= (assoc (:window entry) rd 7) (:window restored)))\n      (is (empty? (:parked restored)))\n      (is (= [nil 7 2] (vm/value (vm/run restored)))))))\n\n\n(deftest ffi-retained\n(deftest image-and-store-context\n  (let [image (:vector (linearize/project (lam '[x] (v 'x))))\n        machine (sr/attach-image (sr/create-vm) image code/contract)\n        address (module/image-identity machine image)\n        closure {:type :closure :params '[x] :entry 2 :segment (get (:code-aliases machine) address)\n                 :env {'captured nil engine/store-of-key :module-store}}\n        marker (module/lift-closure machine closure identity)\n        child (module/spawn-module machine image {:modules (module/default-registry)\n                                                  :origin :child :ancestry ['foo] :capability-secret tu/secret})]\n    (is (module/image-holds? machine image address))\n    (is (not (module/image-holds? machine [[:const 0 9] [:halt 0]] address)))\n    (is (nil? (:control machine)))\n    (is (= {} (:window machine)))\n    (is (= :module-store (:yin.k/store-of marker)))\n    (is (= {'captured nil} (:yin.k/env marker)))\n    (is (= closure (values/payload (module/lower-closure machine marker identity))))\n    (is (= :child (:origin child)))\n    (is (= ['foo] (:ancestry child)))\n    (is (= tu/secret (:capability-secret child)))\n    (is (= :yin.semantic-register/code (:format (module/link-format child))))))\n\n\n(deftest walker-link-parity\n  (let [run (fn [register?]\n  (spawn-module\n    [vm image {:keys [modules origin ancestry capability-secret]}]\n    (load-vector (create-vm\n                   {:primitives (:primitives vm),\n                    :primitive-profiles (:primitive-profiles vm),\n                    :primitive-canonical-names (:primitive-canonical-names vm),\n                    :modules modules,\n                    :make-stream (:make-stream vm),\n                    :link-request (get (:resources vm)\n                                       module/link-request-resource),\n                    :link-response (get (:resources vm)\n                                        module/link-response-resource),\n                    :origin origin,\n                    :ancestry ancestry,\n                    :capability-secret capability-secret,\n                    :secret-source (:secret-source vm),\n                    :attach-stream (:attach-stream vm),\n                    :gc-threshold (:base (:gc vm))})\n                 image\n                 code/contract))\n  (image-identity [_ image] (jing/segment-key image))\n  (image-holds? [_ image segment] (jing/segment-matches? segment image))\n(deftest a-ref-put-on-a-stream-stays-authentic-test\n  (testing \"a ref appended to an in-task stream, unreachable otherwise,\n            survives collections at every allocation and reads back\"\n    (doseq [k (keys builders)]\n      (is (= :pinned\n             (outcome\n               #(run-on\n                  k\n                  (let1 's {:type :stream/make, :buffer 8}\n                        (let1 'cur {:type :stream/cursor, :source (v 's)}\n                              (then (discard {:type :stream/put,\n                                              :target (v 's),\n                                              :val (new-cell (lit :pinned))})\n                                    (then garbage\n                                          (get-cell {:type :stream/next,\n                                                     :source (v 'cur)})))))\n                  1)))\n          (str k)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Determinism and semantics\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private linked-sum\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
